WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:12.000
Average speed is total distance divided by total elapsed time. Use a time greater than zero.

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:24.000
Divide one hundred twenty metres by twenty seconds. The average speed is six metres per second.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:36.000
The walker has an average speed of three metres per second. The cyclist has the greater average speed.

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:48.000
Include stops in elapsed time. Average speed does not mean that the speed was constant at every instant.
